Hand written, applies after the generated rename. The Debian arm64 configuration is for virtio disks;
say so and point to the variables that a real UEFI board needs.

SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 (the licence of the files this patch changes)

diff --git a/configs/debian_arm64_uefi_config b/configs/debian_arm64_uefi_config
index 0ec5bb0..7b1bc23 100644
--- a/configs/debian_arm64_uefi_config
+++ b/configs/debian_arm64_uefi_config
@@ -1,5 +1,11 @@
-# Debian 12 (bookworm) for 64-bit ARM (arm64) with UEFI and GRUB, for virtual machines and for
-# ARM boards with a UEFI firmware.
+# Debian 12 (bookworm) for 64-bit ARM (arm64) with UEFI and GRUB, for virtual machines with a
+# virtio disk (QEMU "virt", cloud hypervisors).
+#
+# This configuration names the disk /dev/vda (OTAPULSE_STORAGE_DEVICE_BASE below) and a serial
+# console of the QEMU "virt" machine. For an ARM board with a UEFI firmware, start from a copy and set
+# OTAPULSE_STORAGE_DEVICE_BASE to its disk (for example /dev/nvme0n1p), or set OTAPULSE_ENABLE_PARTUUID=y
+# together with OTAPULSE_BOOT_PART, OTAPULSE_ROOTFS_PART_A, OTAPULSE_ROOTFS_PART_B and
+# OTAPULSE_DATA_PART (/dev/disk/by-partuuid/... paths), and change the console arguments.
 #
 # Input: the "genericcloud" or "nocloud" arm64 image of Debian 12, for example
 #
